From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ysfaculty <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 15:34:30 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 154/161] hjviewer: delete the account in the app (1.9.1, B1)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Settings → Account offers [계정 삭제] while logged in: at the bottom of the
desktop account card (a quiet button in the danger colour) and as the last
tile of the phone's account section. Its confirmation says what goes (the
PCs of My PCs and their password-less connections, every logged-in device,
the device list, relay approvals and wake requests) and what stays (login
records without the portal ID for 6 months, backups for 14 days), the PCs'
line on a staff-only server, and takes the word '삭제' ('delete' in English)
before its filled danger button sends POST /api/hjv/account/delete with
{"confirm":"delete-account"}, signed by H13 as the other self-service
requests (no new bridge function). While it waits, the bar shows and
nothing closes the dialog; a second press sends nothing.

On hjv-api's 200 with "deleted":true, Rust's H14 logs this device out as an
explicit logout does (the account key, the device list, the login's ticket,
a PC this user's login bound unbinds in one write) and drops the token and
the user, so that no request of the screens goes out with a token whose key
is gone. The screens then reset to logged out without L4, and a result
dialog says that the other devices log out the next time they reach the
server. A 401 closes the dialog for L4, whose reason now names a deleted
account too ("…, 계정이 삭제되었거나, …"); L4 waits for the deletion's
answer rather than coming over its dialog. A 404 (an hjv-api without the
path) says the app cannot delete it now; other answers show hjv-api's own
words and leave the dialog to try again.

The texts are HjvTexts pairs, as all of the account screens' (the
contract's D8; src/lang stays as it is).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
